te-ai-tool-ratings","matchMethod":"none","newText":"UNC Charlotte OneIT rates some campus AI tools as approved for use with data handling guidelines, while AI detection software and AI grading software are listed as Do Not Use.","sourceUrls":["https://oneit.charlotte.edu/innovation/artificial-intelligence/ai-software-guidance/"]},{"id":"claim:claim-unc-charlotte-ctl-not-university-policy","category":"tracker_addition","theme":"source_status","claimId":"claim-unc-charlotte-ctl-not-university-policy","matchMethod":"none","newText":"UNC Charlotte's Center for Teaching and Learning says its AI syllabus guide provides flexible course-level examples and does not provide or use a university-created AI policy.","sourceUrls":["https://teaching.charlotte.edu/teaching-support/teaching-guides/syllabus-guidelines-ai-coursework/"]},{"id":"claim:claim-unc-charlotte-faculty-ai-communication","category":"tracker_addition","theme":"teaching","claimId":"claim-unc-charlotte-faculty-ai-communication","matchMethod":"none","newText":"UNC Charlotte Student Accountability & Conflict Resolution recommends that faculty clearly communicate what AI use is permitted in courses, academic exercises, or assessments, and identifies written notice about how and when AI tools may be used as a best practice.","sourceUrls":["https://accountability.charlotte.edu/artificial-intelligence/"]},{"id":"source_added:https://accountability.charlotte.edu/artificial-intelligence/","category":"source_update","theme":"sources","matchMethod":"source_claim_type","sourceUrls":["https://accountability.charlotte.edu/artificial-intelligence/"]},{"id":"source_added:https://oneit.charlotte.edu/innovation/artificial-intelligence/ai-software-guidance/","category":"source_update","theme":"sources","matchMethod":"source_claim_type","sourceUrls":["https://oneit.charlotte.edu/innovation/artificial-intelligence/ai-software-guidance/"]},{"id":"source_added:https://oneit.charlotte.edu/innovation/artificial-intelligence/security-chec